on flaw (CVE-2026-115560) affecting specific configurations just days after PHP2Shell. Learn how to disable the vulnerable feature and hunt for exploitation.\n [link] https://securityarsenal.com/blog/cve-2026-115560-php-web-server-code-execution-risk-immediate-hardening-guide\n [webpage 3 end]\n[webpage 4 begin] [title] CVE-2026-115560 - Exploits & Severity - Feedly\n [description] 4 days ago · The PHP project has identified a vulnerability in its session upload progress feature, affecting fully patched versions, including 8.5.12, with a fix scheduled for the next regular release.\n [link] https://feedly.com/cve/CVE-2026-115560\n [webpage 4 end]\n\n            \n        ```\n    *   **漏洞利用代码：**\n        ```\n        /tmp/32d58dc881a5b1e186e399e7043551df/AGENTS.md\n---\n# Agents — PHP2Shell unchained\n\nSteuerung: `vtbw-php2shell-lab` oder MCP **`php2shell-unchained`**.\n\n1. Lies `docs/CURSOR-INTEGRATION.md` und `.cursor/skills/php2shell-unchained/SKILL.md`.\n2. Menüpfad: `[1]` FPM, dann `[2]` Zer061 oder `[3]` Jackalsyn, danach `[6]` Sliver C2 / `[7]` Singularity. Sec-Team `[8]` Patch-Audit.\n3. `lab_exploit_map` vor gemischten Pfaden. `zer061-shell` (Kit) ≠ `reverse-shell` (lukechilds, `[5]`) ≠ `sliver` (C2, `[6]`).\n4. Sliver/Tunnel immer mit Ops-Logging (`out/sliver/ops.log`, `out/tunnel/ops.log`); Tunnel-URL dem User zeigen.\n5. Nur Lab oder ausdrücklich erlaubte Ziele. Singularity nicht in PHP-Containern laden.\n\n\n---\n/tmp/32d58dc881a5b1e186e399e7043551df/CONTRIBUTING.md\n---\n# Contributing\n\nThank you for helping improve PHP2Shell Unchained as a **defensive** lab.\n\n## Principles\n\n1. **Lab-only defaults** — no auto-download of weaponized bundles; `fetch-*` scripts remain explicit.\n2. **Document behavior, not opinions** — technical docs describe what the tool does; mitigations are referenced from vendor advisories.\n3. **Reproducibility** — new scenarios need a clear audit ID, log line in `patch_audit.py` or workarounds step, and doc cross-links.\n\n## Development setup\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/Leviticus-Triage/php2shell-unchained.git\ncd php2shell-unchained\n./scripts/install-commands.sh\nvtbw-php2shell-doctor\n```\n\n## Pull requests\n\n- Keep changes focused; match existing shell/Python style in `scripts/` and `attacker/`.\n- Update `docs/DOCUMENTATION.md` and README tables when adding commands or audit IDs.\n- Do not commit `out/`, `third_party/` payloads, or secrets.\n\n## CI\n\nGitHub Actions runs lightweight shell syntax checks on `scripts/` (see `.github/workflows/ci.yml`).\n\n\n---\n/tmp/32d58dc881a5b1e186e399e7043551df/LICENSE\n---\nMIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 Leviticus-Triage\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.\n\n\n---\n/tmp/32d58dc881a5b1e186e399e7043551df/README-PORTABLE.md\n---\n# PHP2Shell — unchained (Portable Paket)\n\n**By Leviticus-Triage**\n\n## 1. Entpacken\n\n```bash\ntar -xzf php2shell-lab-vtbw-portable-*.tar.gz -C ~/Schreibtisch/\ncd ~/Schreibtisch/php2shell-lab-vtbw-portable-*\nchmod +x vtbw-php2shell-lab php2shell-unchained vtbw-php2shell-doctor\n```\n\n## 2. Menü starten\n\n```bash\n./php2shell-unchained\n```\n\nVollständige Schritt-für-Schritt-Anleitung:  \n`php2shell-lab-vtbw/docs/HOWTO-DE.md`\n\n## 3. Bundles (Internet nötig, einmalig)\n\n```bash\n./vtbw-php2shell-lab fetch-zer061\n./vtbw-php2shell-lab fetch-jackalsyn\n./vtbw-php2shell-lab fetch-reverse-shell    # optional\ncd php2shell-lab-vtbw && docker compose --profile tools build attacker\n```\n\n## 4. Kurz-Workflows\n\n| Ziel | Befehle |\n|------|---------|\n| Interaktiv www-data (FPM) | `up` → `test` → `shell` |\n| Heap-RCE mod_php | `apache-up` → `zer061` → `zer061-shell` |\n| Jackalsyn | `fetch-jackalsyn` → `up` → `jackalsyn selftest` → `jackalsyn lab` |\n| 2 Targets scannen | `apache-multi-up` → `scan` |\n\n## 5. Paketinhalt\n\n```\nphp2shell-lab-vtbw-portable-<datum>/\n├── php2shell-unchained      # Menü\n├── vtbw-php2shell-lab       # alle CLI-Befehle (siehe: help)\n├── vtbw-php2shell-doctor\n├── README-PORTABLE.md       # diese Datei\n└── php2shell-lab-vtbw/      # Docker-Lab + docs/\n    ├── README.md\n    ├── docs/HOWTO-DE.md\n    ├── docker-compose.yml\n    ├── scripts/\n    └── targets/lab-targets.txt\n```\n\n**Nicht im Archiv** (nach Entpacken laden): `third_party/zer061-php2shell`, `php-up-2026`, `reverse-shell`, `jackalsyn-reup`.\n\n## 6. Hinweise\n\n- Lab-Netzwerk ist **internal** (kein Internet aus Containern).\n- Jackalsyn `lab` nutzt FCGI `target:9000` (php-fpm im FPM-Target).\n- Zer061 und Chain-A sind **getrennte** Exploit-Pfade.\n\n\n---\n/tmp/32d58dc881a5b1e186e399e7043551df/README.md\n---\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <strong>PHP2Shell Unchained</strong><br>\n  <em>Isolated adversary-emulation lab for PHP Session Upload Progress (PHP2Shell) chains, mitigations, and blue-team validation</em>\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://g\n        ```\n\n    **你的角色：** 你是一名专业的网络安全分析师，擅长分析CVE漏洞信息。\n\n    **任务：**\n\n    1.  **CVE有效性：** 分析此CVE是否为真实存在的有效漏洞。请综合考虑CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在、漏洞的技术细节等因素。\n    2.  **POC有效性：** 判断提供的POC代码是否有效，是否能实际利用此漏洞，并分析其有效性。\n    3.  **投毒风险：** 分析POC代码内容,判断此仓库中是否存在作者隐藏的投毒代码,分析结果使用百分比。务必不要把POC验证的后门代码判定为投毒代码。\n    4.  **利用方式：** 详细分析并总结漏洞的利用方式，包括攻击步骤、所需条件等。\n    5.  **代码分析：** 详细分析POC代码的工作原理、关键组件和执行流程。\n    6.  **排序优先级:** 搜索引擎结果 >  漏洞利用代码 > 漏洞库信息\n    7.  **输出内容:** 务必使用中文\n    8.  **markdown内容:** 务必使用markdown格式，包含以下部分：\n        - 漏洞概述\n        - 有效性分析\n        - 投毒风险分析\n        - 利用方式\n        - 代码分析\n    **输出格式：**  你**必须**严格按照以下 **JSON** 格式输出，**不要包含任何额外的文字、说明或前缀/后缀**。JSON中的**所有键和字符串类型的值必须使用双引号**。请务必对特殊字符进行转义。\n\n    **示例JSON:**```json\n    {\n        \"name\": \"CVE-2023-12345-ExampleApp-SQL注入\",\n        \"type\": \"SQL注入\",\n        \"app\": \"ExampleApp\", \n        \"risk\": \"高危，可能导致数据泄露和远程代码执行\",\n        \"version\": \"<= 1.0\",\n        \"condition\": \"需要网络访问和数据库端口开放\",\n        \"poc_available\": \"是\",\n        \"poison\": \"90%\",\n        \"cve_valid\": \"是\",\n        \"markdown\": \"# 漏洞概述\n\n该漏洞存在于ExampleApp的登录模块,攻击者可以通过构造恶意的SQL语句绕过身份验证...\n\n## 有效性分析\n\n根据CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在等因素，该CVE是真实有效的...\n\n## 投毒风险分析\n\n该仓库存在较高的投毒风险，主要原因是...\n\n## 利用方式\n\n1.  攻击者需要网络访问权限\n2.  构造恶意的SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  绕过身份验证，获取系统访问权限\n\n## 代码分析\n\n主要代码组件包括：\n- `exploit.py`: 主漏洞利用脚本\n- `payloads.py`: 包含各种SQL注入payload\n- `utils.py`: 辅助工具函数\n\n代码执行流程：\n1.  连接到目标数据库\n2.  构造恶意SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  解析响应，获取敏感信息\n\",\n        \"repo_name\": \"example/repo\",\n        \"repo_url\": \"https://github.com/example/repo\",\n        \"cve_url\": \"https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2023-12345\"\n    }\n        ",
